  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Goalkeeper – start the counter",
  "description": "Two goalkeepers and a coach or outfield player with balls. One keeper is in goal, the other is the counter-attacker and stands at the corner of the box. The coach stands at an angle in front of goal.\n\nThe coach plays the ball in front of goal from different spots: shots, low balls and high crosses. The keeper catches or saves. As soon as the keeper has the ball, the counter-attacker sprints towards the halfway line, and the keeper must find the run beyond halfway – with a throw, a goal kick from the hands or a side volley. The ball goes ahead of the player, not to their feet.\n\nSwap roles after six balls. Variant: the coach plays a back pass instead, and the keeper takes the ball to the side and plays the counter pass with the foot. Switch the counter-attacker to the other side too. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Secure the ball first – a dropped ball means no counter."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look up as soon as you have the ball and see where the run is going."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Put the ball ahead of the player so they can take it on at full speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Pick the right distribution: throw when it is close and safe, kick when it is far."
    }
  ],
